<title>UK: UK'S Major sees jobless rate falling further.</title>
<headline>UK'S Major sees jobless rate falling further.</headline>
<dateline>ABERDEEN, Scotland 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major said on Wednesday he saw no sign of an end to the falling trend in British unemployment.</p>
<p>Speaking at an election rally for supporters of his Conservative party, Major contrasted &quot;distressingly high&quot; unemployment rates in continental Europe of 10 to 12 percent with the situation in Britain &quot;as we move down towards six percent with every indication that its going to go on falling, putting more and more of our people back into work.&quot;</p>
</text>
